<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2864" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Antĭgŏnus</span></b> , i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀντίγονος</span>.
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The name of several kings after Alexander the
			Great.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Antigonus I., <i>father of Demetrius Poliorcetes</i>, <i><span class="en">Nep. Eum. 5,
			7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Off. 2, 14, 48</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Just.
			13</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			Antigonus Gonatas, <i>son of Demetrius
			Poliorcetes</i>, <i><span class="en">Just. 17, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">24, 1
			al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			Antigonus Doson, <i><span class="en">Liv. 40, 54</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Just. 28,
			3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Of other persons.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Antigonus <i>of Cymœ</i>, <i>a writer on
			Agriculture</i>, <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 1, 8</span></i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 1, 1,
			9</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A plastic artist</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 34, 8,
				19, § 84</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<i>A messenger of king Deiotarus</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Deiot.
				15, 41</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>D.</b>
			<i>A Roman freedman</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				13, 33</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
